What:		/sys/devices/platform/<mem-dump-device>/core_reg_num
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	Yushan Li <yushan.li@oss.qualcomm.com>
Description:	(RW) Number of per-core CPU subsystem (CPUSS) registers to
		reserve space for in the register dump table.

		Read returns the currently configured count in decimal.

		Write accepts a hexadecimal value. The write fails with
		-EPERM if any per-core or system register has already been
		configured via register_config, since changing the count
		afterwards would invalidate the existing layout. It fails
		with -EINVAL or -ENOMEM if the requested count does not
		leave enough reserved dump memory for the fixed table
		header.

What:		/sys/devices/platform/<mem-dump-device>/register_config
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	Yushan Li <yushan.li@oss.qualcomm.com>
Description:	(RW) Configuration of the CPUSS registers to be captured in
		the register dump.

		Read returns the list of currently configured registers,
		one per line, first the per-core registers under a
		"per-core registers:" header and then the system registers
		under a "system registers:" header. Each register line has
		the form:

			0xOFFSET, 0xVALUE, TYPE

		where TYPE is one of:

			r - single register read
			w - register write
			d - delay
			R - repeated read

		Write accepts:

			OFFSET VALUE CMD [PER_CORE]

		as hexadecimal OFFSET and VALUE, a single command
		character CMD (one of 'r', 'w', 'd', 'R'), and an optional
		decimal PER_CORE flag (0 or 1, default 0) selecting whether
		the register applies per-core or system-wide. OFFSET must
		be 4-byte aligned. Fails with -EINVAL on malformed input or
		an unsupported command, and with -ENOMEM if there is not
		enough reserved dump memory left to add the entry.

What:		/sys/devices/platform/<mem-dump-device>/register_reset
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	Yushan Li <yushan.li@oss.qualcomm.com>
Description:	(WO) Resets the CPUSS register dump table to its default
		state, discarding any registers added via register_config
		and restoring the default per-core register count.

		Write accepts only the value 1; any other value fails with
		-EINVAL.

What:		/sys/devices/platform/<mem-dump-device>/format_version
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	Yushan Li <yushan.li@oss.qualcomm.com>
Description:	(RO) Format version of the CPUSS register dump data
		currently stored in the dump memory, returned as a decimal
		integer.

What:		/sys/devices/platform/<mem-dump-device>/spr_config
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	Yushan Li <yushan.li@oss.qualcomm.com>
Description:	(RW) Configuration of the per-CPU SPR (Special Purpose
		Register) dump data.

		Read returns, for each CPU that has SPR dump memory
		initialized, a "spr data for CPU[N] below:" header followed
		by the list of currently configured SPR data values, one
		per line.

		Write accepts:

			SPR_DATA CPU_NUM

		as two decimal integers: the SPR data value to append and
		the target CPU number. Fails with -EINVAL if CPU_NUM is out
		of range, and with -ENOMEM if there is not enough reserved
		SPR dump memory left for that CPU.

What:		/sys/devices/platform/<mem-dump-device>/sprs_register_reset
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	Yushan Li <yushan.li@oss.qualcomm.com>
Description:	(WO) Resets the SPR dump tables for all CPUs, discarding any
		data added via spr_config.

		Write accepts only the value 1; any other value fails with
		-EINVAL.

What:		/sys/devices/platform/<mem-dump-device>/sprs_format_version
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	Yushan Li <yushan.li@oss.qualcomm.com>
Description:	(RO) Format version of the SPR dump data currently stored in
		the dump memory for each initialized CPU, returned one line
		per CPU as "SPR data format version for cpuN is VERSION".
